  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it, build it or look at a frame, so the visuals are untested. The scene is a paper-style bird flying a circle over a ground disc with trees and rocks.\n\n- **Bird:** an ellipsoid body, a head with a cone beak and two eyes with pupils, and a 5-feather tail fan. Each wing has an inner and an outer box segment, hinged at the shoulder and elbow.\n- **Flight:** an 8-second loop with a 6-unit radius at constant height. The bird always faces its direction of travel and banks about 0.32 rad into the turn. Flapping is 2 Hz, so each lap holds exactly 16 flaps and the loop closes with no jump. The outer wing lags the inner by 0.8 rad, which makes the wing bend. The body bobs ±0.08 units, highest near the bottom of the downstroke.\n- **World:** a sky-blue background, a hemisphere light, a neutral environment and one shadow-casting directional light. Trees (a trunk plus two cones) stand inside and outside the flight circle, with three rocks.\n- **Camera:** it follows the bird at 12 units from the center, outside the circle, 0.5 rad behind it, at height 5, and looks at the bird.\n- **Readiness:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frames render.\n\nI'm least sure of three things:\n- **Bank direction:** I derived the sign by hand.\n- **Beak direction:** I assumed the cone's tip points along +Y.\n- **Shadow `fit` option:** I set it to cover the ground, and I'm not sure the engine honors it.\n\nI also left out the per-frame camera cut (`cut: true`) so the camera isn't reset each frame.",
